This document contains the minutes of an institutional ethics review board meeting conducted on October 14th, 2023. The meeting was convened to assess proposed faculty changes and ensure alignment with institutional governance standards.

\section{Discussion}

The meeting began with a review of proposed faculty changes that were submitted by Dr. Elena Rodriguez, Associate Professor of Mathematics. The proposed adjustments included:

\begin{itemize}
\item Curriculum modifications for advanced calculus sequences
\item Alternative delivery formats for online courses
\item Removal of mandatory teaching assistants
\item Requirement for faculty to maintain 20% of their weekly teaching load
\end{itemize}

Discussion focused on:
- Whether these changes adequately address the stated learning outcomes
- Whether alternative delivery models are feasible given course enrollment numbers
- Whether workload changes would reduce staff burnout

Dr. Rodriguez presented her case to the board. The board expressed support for the curriculum adjustments but noted concerns regarding the 20% requirement. One participant, Dr. James Chen, raised a safety concern regarding course eligibility restrictions. The full board voted to schedule a separate session to review the safety concerns.

\section{Next Steps}

Following the meeting, the following actions were recommended:

1. Review the curriculum changes with departmental chair
2. Schedule a consultation with the Office of Research Ethics to review workload allocation
3. Update faculty handbook language on teaching requirements
4. Launch a pilot program for alternative delivery formats

The board will convene a second vote at the next scheduled meeting.

\section{Conclusion}

The meeting concluded with:

- A consensus recommendation to approve the proposed changes
- An invitation to schedule follow-up sessions if needed
- A commitment to maintaining open communication channels

Dr. Khan expressed appreciation for the opportunity to address governance concerns.

